# CODEOWNERS - required reviewers for protected paths (t_537e2195)
#
# Syntax: <path-pattern> <owner...>  (gitignore-style globs, owners are
# @user or @org/team handles that MUST have write access to this repo).
# The LAST matching pattern for a file wins.
#
# Owner note: @AlexeyZelenin is currently the only GitHub account with
# write access to this repo (the fork these zeus/* PRs target). No team
# exists yet; when one is added, replace the individual with @org/team so
# the review gate can be satisfied by someone other than the PR author.
#
# The file alone does not block merges - a branch-protection rule / ruleset
# on `main` with "Require review from Code Owners" enabled must be turned on
# for these owners to be requested and required on PRs.

# --- Database migrations -----------------------------------------------------
# Any change under a top-level migrations/ tree (schema history is high-risk).
migrations/**            @AlexeyZelenin

# --- OpenAPI specs -----------------------------------------------------------
# Unanchored pattern: matches openapi.json / openapi.yaml / an openapi/ dir
# in ANY directory of the repo (API contract changes need owner sign-off).
openapi*                 @AlexeyZelenin

# --- Protect this policy itself ---------------------------------------------
# So the protection cannot be weakened without owner review.
/.github/CODEOWNERS      @AlexeyZelenin
